[
    {
        "content": "<p>Hi, I'm trying to figure out how to idiomatically build <code>Decidable</code> instances from <code>Prop</code> definitions that essentially provide the decision procedure as part of the definition with pattern matching. Concretely, something like this: </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FooBar</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FooBar</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FooBar</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FooBar</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FooBar</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isFoo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FooBar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">False</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- instance (fb : FooBar): Decidable fb.isFoo := inferInstance</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- failed to synthesize instance of type class</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">--  Decidable fb.isFoo</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Here if I replace <code>Prop</code> with <code>Bool</code> and <code>True/False</code> with <code>true/false</code> I just get a regular computable boolean function. I would expect it should be straightforward to derive the <code>Decidable</code> instances (I find the version of defining everything over <code>Bool</code> and then \"lifting\" to <code>Prop</code> via <code>= true</code> to be kind of ugly/unidiomatic). Is there a way to derive these automatically that I'm missing? If not, is this something that would make sense to define myself similar to a derivingHandler?</p>",
        "id": 587771764,
        "sender_full_name": "Andrés Goens",
        "timestamp": 1776693086
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I was just contemplating this exact question this weekend. I have some definitions that could equally well be inductively defined propositions, <code>Prop</code>-valued functions, or <code>Bool</code>-valued functions, and it's inconvenient that you don't get all three. As far as I know, there's no derivation system yet for this in any library.</p>\n<p>A way to idiomatically do this is to translate the definition from a <code>Prop</code>-valued one into a <code>Bool</code>-valued one systematically, prove the equivalence, and then define the instance, like so:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FooBar</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FooBar</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FooBar</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FooBar</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FooBar</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isFoo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FooBar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">False</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FooBar</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isFoo'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FooBar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bool</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FooBar</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isFoo'_eq_true_iff</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FooBar</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FooBar</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isFoo'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FooBar</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isFoo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">cases</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;;&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">FooBar</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isFoo'</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FooBar</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isFoo</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FooBar</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Decidable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">FooBar</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isFoo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">decidable_of_bool</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FooBar</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isFoo'_eq_true_iff</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>If you have a recursive definition, then you'll need a more complicated proof. I've found <code>fun_induction</code> to be helpful for this, since you want to induct on the recursive structure of the definitions, <em>not</em> the arguments themselves, at least for the general case (ones that don't do some simple structural recursion).</p>",
        "id": 587829115,
        "sender_full_name": "Kyle Miller",
        "timestamp": 1776708112
    }
